      "subject": "Why I wrote No Blue Sky — {{name}}",
      "body": "Hi {{name}},\n\nEvery story starts somewhere. For the No Blue Sky series, it started with a question that wouldn't let me go: What would it really take for humans to build a civilization on Mars?\n\nI've always been fascinated by space exploration — not just the rockets and the science, but the human side of it. The courage it takes to leave everything behind. The grit required to survive in a place that wasn't made for us. The hope that drives people to build something new, even when the odds are impossible.\n\nI spent years researching Mars colonization — the real science, the engineering challenges, the psychology of long-term isolation. But the books aren't just about technology. They're about people: families, leaders, dreamers, and rebels trying to create a home on a world with no blue sky.\n\nBuilt from Dust, the first volume, is closest to my heart. It follows the first wave of settlers as they land on Mars and face the brutal reality of survival. Everything they thought they knew is tested. Everything they believed is challenged.\n\n🎁 Reply with \"SAMPLE\" and I'll send you the first chapter of Built from Dust — free, no strings attached. Experience the landing for yourself.\n\nMore soon,\nBob Mills",
