      "subject": "What educators and readers are saying, {{name}}",
      "body": "Hi {{name}},\n\nOver the past year, the No Blue Sky series has found an unexpected home in classrooms and book clubs across the country. Here's what people are saying:\n\n📖 \"Built from Dust is the first book in years that got my reluctant readers excited about science fiction. The Mars setting hooks them, but the characters keep them reading.\"\n— Jennifer T., High School English Teacher\n\n📖 \"We used The Oxygen Gamble as part of our STEM literacy unit. Students were designing their own Mars colony proposals while we read. The cross-curricular engagement was incredible.\"\n— Marcus D., Middle School Science Coordinator\n\n📖 \"The Red Charter sparked some of the best classroom debates I've ever facilitated — about governance, resource allocation, and what a fair society looks like.\"\n— Dr. Lisa Chen, University Lecturer\n\n⭐ \"Built from Dust grabbed me from the first page. Bob Mills writes with urgency and heart.\"\n— Amazon Review\n\n⭐ \"Each volume gets better. Rivers Under Mars had me on the edge of my seat.\"\n— Goodreads Review\n\n🏆 The No Blue Sky series has been featured in Indie Sci-Fi Monthly's \"Best of the Year\" roundup and recommended by educators for STEM and literacy programs.\n\nMany schools and libraries order the full set for their collections. Others start with a single volume to test the waters — and come back for more.\n\nWhether you're buying for yourself or for a group, I'm here to help you find the right fit. Just reply with any questions.\n\nBest,\nBob Mills",
